<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
  <header class="mb-10">
    <p class="apx-mono-label">APX / Frequently asked questions</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-apx-text sm:text-4xl">
      How the policy analytics platform works
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-apx-muted">
      APX connects source-linked claims and positions with policy proposals, voting, delegation, and
      verification. It is decision support—not a government service or a representative survey.
    </p>
  </header>

  <dl class="divide-y divide-apx-line border-y border-apx-line">
    <div id="what-is-apx" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">What is APX?</dt>
      <dd class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          APX—Sovereign Policy Analytics &amp; Expert Consensus Engine—is a policy analytics project
          for organizing claims, proposals, public positions, sources, and participation. Its focus
          includes AI governance, sovereign technology, cyber risk, and information operations.
        </p>
        <p>
          The platform records positions and votes. It does not treat popularity as proof, claim
          that its participants represent all experts, or make binding decisions for public bodies.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div id="delegation" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">How does liquid democracy work here?</dt>
      <dd class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          A signed-in participant may vote directly or choose delegates. Unless the participant votes
          directly on a proposal, the delegated answer follows the majority of the selected delegates
          who have recorded a vote. If those delegate votes are tied, no delegated vote is recorded.
          A direct vote always takes precedence.
        </p>
        <p>
          Delegation is optional and currently applies across issues rather than by topic. A
          delegate's public positions can be inferred from sourced statements; that does not mean
          the delegate personally voted on APX.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div id="sourced-positions" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">How are sources and positions handled?</dt>
      <dd class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          Records connect quotations and claims to authors, dates, policy statements, and source
          URLs. Readers can follow those links to inspect context. Third-party quotations and
          reporting remain attributable to their original publishers and rights holders.
        </p>
        <p>
          Verification distinguishes whether a quote is authentic, whether it is relevant to a
          statement, and whether an inferred vote matches the opinion. Automated checks may be
          mistaken or inconclusive; a verification badge is not a universal certificate of truth.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div id="intelligence" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">What is the intelligence hub?</dt>
      <dd class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          The <.link href={~p"/intelligence"} class="font-semibold text-apx-cyan underline">APX intelligence hub</.link>
          curates public RSS and Atom metadata from selected policy, technology, and security
          publishers. Rule-based triage produces a three-bullet brief, a heuristic impact label,
          extracted feed claims, and possible links to existing APX proposals.
        </p>
        <p>
          It stores a short excerpt and the canonical publisher URL, not full news articles. The
          ratings are not official threat assessments. Readers should open the source and check for
          context, corrections, and later reporting.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div id="verification-language" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">What do the APX terms mean?</dt>
      <dd class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-apx-text">Empirical Consensus Metrics</strong> means summaries of
          recorded views and disagreement—not a claim that a group is representative or that any
          fixed share of auditors agrees.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-apx-text">Non-Deterministic System Verification</strong> describes
          review processes whose human and automated outcomes can differ. The system exposes the
          status and evidence so it can be challenged.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-apx-text">Sovereign Telemetry</strong> means structured, source-linked
          public policy signals. It is not an official government feed or classified monitoring.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div id="who-is-behind" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">Who is behind APX?</dt>
      <dd class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          APX is developed as a policy analytics project. “APX Epistemic Research Directorate” is an
          editorial label for project research and briefs, not a separate legal entity, registered
          non-profit, government body, or certification authority.
        </p>
        <p>
          APX is intended to be useful to researchers, parliamentarians, committee clerks, and
          sovereign security leads. This describes the intended audience, not a claim of adoption or
          endorsement by those groups.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div id="funding" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">What is the project's funding status?</dt>
      <dd class="text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        APX does not publish an audited funding statement on this site. Contact the project if you
        need current information; no non-profit or charitable status is claimed here.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div id="contribute" class="grid gap-3 py-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-apx-text lg:col-span-4">How can I contribute?</dt>
      <dd class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-apx-muted lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          Add a source, propose a missing perspective, review an existing record, or explore the
          <.link href={~p"/dataset"} class="font-semibold text-apx-cyan underline">public dataset</.link>.
          Use the <.link href={~p"/contact"} class="font-semibold text-apx-cyan underline">contact form</.link>
          to reach the project.
        </p>
        <p>
          The machine-readable MCP tools are documented at
          <.link href={~p"/mcp-tools"} class="font-semibold text-apx-cyan underline">/mcp-tools</.link>.
          Public read-only tools are available without an API key; write operations require an
          authorized key and role.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</div>
